# Copy to `.env` and edit to point at data you have downloaded.
# Every variable is OPTIONAL: unset ones fall back to the original workstation paths
# (which won't exist on your machine — the affected script then fails with a clear error).
#
# Tier-1 reproduction (figures, concordance, held-out score) needs NONE of these — those
# artifacts are committed under data/. You only need these for training, full-corpus
# inference, or regenerating the morphology/bbox-grid photo figures.
# See docs/DATA_AVAILABILITY.md for what each root must contain and where to obtain it.

# OMNRF project data drive (labels DB, video manifests, parquet runs, detect-stores, cutouts)
# SALMONID_PROJECTS_ROOT=/path/to/Projects

# Raw tunnel-camera footage (each root holds Ganaraska/ and Credit/ subdirs)
# SALMONID_FOOTAGE_ROOT=/path/to/RiverWatcher
# SALMONID_FOOTAGE_ROOT_FAST=/path/to/RiverWatcher      # NVMe mirror for throughput
# SALMONID_RECOVERED_ROOT=/path/to/recovered            # 2019 Credit / 2020 Ganaraska archive

# Frozen training COCO datasets (deimv2_fish_6class_masked_v*)
# SALMONID_COCO_CACHE=/path/to/ssl_cache

# External DEIMv2 training repo (Intellindust-AI-Lab/DEIMv2 @ pinned SHA — see docs/DEIMV2_PIN.md)
# SALMONID_DEIM_DIR=/path/to/DEIMv2

# Sibling OMNRF repos holding pre-2024 technician NET counts
# SALMONID_LOMU_INTERVIEW_DIR=/path/to/lomu_interview
# SALMONID_MODEL_PRO_DIR=/path/to/model_pro

# BoT-SORT re-ID weights (boxmot auto-downloads if left as the bare filename)
# SALMONID_REID_WEIGHTS=osnet_x0_25_msmt17.pt
